<title>USA: Homestake says Sante Fe bid too expensive.</title>
<headline>Homestake says Sante Fe bid too expensive.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Homestake Mining Co said Monday it dropped out of the bidding for Santa Fe Pacific Gold Corp because the price got too high and threatened to be dilutive to its earnings.</p>
<p>Homestake was outbid by Newmont Mining Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;The auction got too expensive,&quot; Jack Thompson, Homestake chief executive officer, said in a statement.</p>
<p>Earlier today Santa Fe announced it had agreed to merge with Newmont, which will exchange 0.43 Newmont share for each Santa Fe share.</p>
</text>
